prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D scene-building tool. Users can select lantern and chair models from the toolbar, click the ground to place them, and select, move, and delete placed objects.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to preload assets/Lantern.glb and assets/SheenChair.glb;
(2) After loading is complete, cache the model data for subsequent cloning and placement;
(3) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Scene Layout]
(4) Create a ground plane (PlaneGeometry 20x20, light gray-green 0xC8D6C0), placed horizontally at y=0;
(5) Add a grid guide (GridHelper, 20x20, gray) covering the ground;
(6) Use OrbitControls to control the camera, with a default top-down viewing angle;
(7) AmbientLight (0.5) + DirectionalLight (0.8) + HemisphereLight (sky blue/ground green);

[Toolbar]
(8) The top toolbar contains two buttons:
  - "Place Lantern" (id="placeLanternBtn")
  - "Place Chair" (id="placeChairBtn")
(9) Clicking a toolbar button enters placement mode. At this point, change the mouse cursor to a crosshair and prompt the user to click the ground to place the object;
(10) Click the same button again or press the Escape key to cancel placement mode;

[Placement Interaction]
(11) In placement mode, use Raycaster to detect the intersection between the mouse ray and the ground;
(12) After clicking the ground, clone and place the corresponding model at the intersection position (Lantern scale 0.02, SheenChair scale 3);
(13) Exit placement mode after placement;
(14) For each object placed, objectCount += 1;

[Selection and Operations]
(15) In non-placement mode, click a placed object to select it;
(16) The selected object receives an outline highlight effect (an emissive color or an edge/wireframe mode may be used);
(17) After selecting an object, use the arrow keys (ArrowUp/Down/Left/Right) to move it by 0.5 units per keypress;
(18) Press the Delete key to delete the selected object, objectCount -= 1;
(19) Click an empty area to clear the selection;

[HUD Display]
(20) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Number of placed objects (id="objectCount")
  - Current mode (id="currentMode", "browse" / "place_lantern" / "place_chair")
  - Selected object information (id="selectedInfo", type + position, or "None")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether model preloading is complete)
  - objectCount: number (total number of placed objects)
  - currentMode: string ("browse" / "place_lantern" / "place_chair")
  - selectedObject: { type: string, position: {x, y, z} } | null (selected object information)
  - lanternCount: number (number of lanterns)
  - chairCount: number (number of chairs)

Output a single standalone HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
